            <ArticleTitle>[The informative value of pericardial fluid electrolytes and glucose in acute forms of coronary heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The informative value of the levels of calcium, potassium, sodium, magnesium, and glucose was estimated in individuals who had suddenly died from acute coronary insufficiency or acute myocardial infarction in the prenecrotic phase. The informational variations in the concentrations of electrolytes and glucose were found to reflect the differences available in the pathogenesis of an ischemic process in acute coronary insufficiency and acute myocardial infarction in the prenecrotic phase.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
